<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<map xmlns="http://openorienteering.org/apps/mapper/xml/v2" version="9">
    <notes>INFO (course setter to include on map)
Title:
	Northern part: Canterbury Park
	Southen part: Nga Puna Wai
Scale: 1:4,000
Contour interval: 2.5m
North lines: 250m apart


CREDITS (course setter to include on map - 6pt Arial)
Cartography: Initial by L. Earnshaw 2010.  Extended South by N. Smith 2020
Updates: C. Forne 2014, N. Smith 2016, R. Moore 2021, S. Smith 2023, R. Moore 2024, A. Moore 2024.
Copyright © Peninsula and Plains Orienteers
Possession of this map does not imply right of access
Non-commercial use only unless otherwise granted
Map version: becf920


COORDINATORS' NOTES (map coordinator to update + commit on map being sent)
Last sent to: Thomas Zinzan &lt;thomas.zinzans@gmail.com&gt;


CONTROLLERS' NOTES (controller to read upon map being sent)
Need to check gates marked with purple crossing point symbol, locks are added and removed regularly.
Possibility that all courses need to be approved 2-3 weeks before event with CCC (see permissions).
Areas to the west may be booked for dog and horse events - planner to check with landowner.
Hazards include traffic, mountain bikers, pedestrians, lake, river, prickly bushes, horses, dogs.


MAPPERS' NOTES</notes>
